# __APP_NAME__

The purpose of this app, its users and its terms belong at the top of this document. The sections below
describe the structure that `mpfrontend create app` wrote.

## Routes

- `/` opens the catalog list (`src/app/page.tsx`).
- `/catalog` is the catalog list screen; its page and its search are URL state, so the screen can be
  linked and refreshed (`src/app/catalog/page.tsx`).
- `/catalog/[position]` is the detail screen of one item, a child route of the list
  (`src/app/catalog/[position]/page.tsx`).
- `/components` shows the framework components (`src/app/components/page.tsx`).

## Layout

- `src/app/` holds thin routes, the root layout and route handlers only.
- `src/features/<feature>/` holds one user workflow: `ui/`, `model/`, `hooks/`, `api/`, `utils/` and its
  `index.ts` public entry. Code outside a feature imports only that `index.ts`; lint refuses a deeper
  import.
- `src/entities/<entity>/` holds the types and rules that the features of one entity share.
- `src/api/generated/` holds generated contracts; `src/api/server/` holds the hand-written server
  boundary beside them.
- `src/config/` holds validated configuration; `src/theme/` holds the theme registry.

## Languages

The app starts with English only (`en`, left to right, the default), and its `lang` and `dir` follow the
locale registry in `src/config/app.ts`. To add a locale in this repository:

1. Register it with its direction, `'<code>': { direction: 'ltr' }` or `'<code>': { direction: 'rtl' }`, and
   a `numberingSystem` when its digits differ from the default.
2. Add `messages/<code>.ts` next to `messages/en.ts` in every catalog set, typed
   `Translation<typeof base>`, and list it in the `translations` of that set.
3. Run the `catalog-check` target: it names every set that lacks the catalog or a key.

To use another locale instead of English, register only that locale and make it `defaultLocale`, rename
every `messages/en.ts` to `messages/<code>.ts` with the text of that locale, and set the base import and
`defaultLocale` of every set to `<code>`. New features then start from that locale's catalog.

Add a feature with `mpfrontend create feature`, a screen with `mpfrontend create route` and a package
that two apps need with `mpfrontend create package`; see the CLI guide of MP Frontend.

Business rules go in `docs/business-rules.md` and decisions in `docs/adr/` when the first one exists.
The contracts this app reads are listed in [api-contracts.md](api-contracts.md).
